        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5208e6b0-f468-3e67-b8b0-cdf4ec3c1da4",
                "word": "RSE",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7b6d59a1-1d97-3eb3-86d8-995730a0f863",
                        "entry_id": "5208e6b0-f468-3e67-b8b0-cdf4ec3c1da4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Responsabilité sociale de l’entreprise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Économie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75f6a0e7-552c-4810-93b7-891eb2d91318",
                                "sense_id": "7b6d59a1-1d97-3eb3-86d8-995730a0f863",
                                "text": "Chez Petit Bateau, cette démarche s’inscrit dans une volonté d’éco-responsabilité et des engagements RSE forts parmi lesquels une production vertueuse, au plus près de la demande."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f9a5cb1-705f-433e-869c-ca8080a34a3b",
                                "sense_id": "7b6d59a1-1d97-3eb3-86d8-995730a0f863",
                                "text": "Alors que le burn-out touche 34 % des salariés, comme le relevait en début d’année le service de téléconsultation Medadom, citant une enquête de l’Observatoire de la responsabilité sociétale des entreprises (RSE), le management bienveillant est donc désormais sur toutes les lèvres."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5bd2efb6-70d1-4ef9-b5c5-329db75acbe6",
                        "source_entry_id": "5208e6b0-f468-3e67-b8b0-cdf4ec3c1da4",
                        "source_sense_id": "7b6d59a1-1d97-3eb3-86d8-995730a0f863",
                        "target_lang_word": "corporate social responsibility",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "corporate social responsibility",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4ed1609-9a4b-3583-9b49-a30edf90e785",
                                        "entry_id": "a7c64137-cf40-3c16-a8ff-fde0d2798330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of international private business self-regulation which aims to contribute to societal goals of a philanthropic, activist, or charitable nature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59010a99-5ae9-4530-9af9-b28af55d3059",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ed1609-9a4b-3583-9b49-a30edf90e785",
                                                "text": "Far too often, those defending or advocating for corporate social responsibility are interested in diminishing the status of capitalism, profit seeking, self-interest, and/or neoclassical economics. But I think one can embrace corporate social responsibility without this baggage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70041cb1-118e-4b8b-80d9-cd820c1b3026",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ed1609-9a4b-3583-9b49-a30edf90e785",
                                                "text": "The company's move isn't an act of corporate social responsibility—it’s a response to labor economics that others may soon follow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15a20fed-8f3b-4a34-8165-ab5bcb41f64a",
                                                "sense_id": "d4ed1609-9a4b-3583-9b49-a30edf90e785",
                                                "text": "There are normally anti-embarrassment clauses in such arrangements and, from a corporate social responsibility point of view, the upside of standing by a tarnished individual is often outweighed by the downside."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8441ebce-4aad-4110-ab06-ad747b2d377e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5208e6b0-f468-3e67-b8b0-cdf4ec3c1da4",
                        "source_sense_id": "7b6d59a1-1d97-3eb3-86d8-995730a0f863",
                        "target_lang_word": "CSR",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "CSR",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df479683-6b16-3c64-a161-c381fd10a896",
                                        "entry_id": "4e14964a-9688-32cd-bfa6-cd031a831bed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of corporate social responsibility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "244d8525-a7de-4373-be65-232153d6f708",
                                                "sense_id": "df479683-6b16-3c64-a161-c381fd10a896",
                                                "text": "He could never have developed GE’s reputation in that sector if he were still fighting the image of stonewalling on Hudson River cleanup efforts. “They've completely jujitsu-ed that,” notes PR executive Richard Edelman. “They've set a new standard. It's not just corporate social responsibility (CSR) as philanthropy. It's CSR that makes money.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ac0a74b-13ae-4ea4-a98e-c9606683cf7d",
                                                "sense_id": "df479683-6b16-3c64-a161-c381fd10a896",
                                                "text": "While there appears to be something to this generalization about millennials and CSR appeals, much more needs to be learned about the nuances of what works and what does not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a5f2369-60f1-4f15-b49b-6e58a329c910",
                                                "sense_id": "df479683-6b16-3c64-a161-c381fd10a896",
                                                "text": "The shackles of CSR have now been tightened by the concept of ESG (Environmental, Social, and corporate Governance)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
